editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:393:- **S2 doorway:** "You came through the board," / "I came through the board." / "Then you already know it doesn't care who you were." / "I'm learning," Vastin said. **S2 close:** "Because a council would file it," Vastin said, "and I spent forty years being the man they sent to make sure the filing held. I know exactly how deep a thing has to be buried before no one goes looking. This is deeper than that." … "I helped bury smaller things. I'd like to dig one up before I'm done." Also: "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." / "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." / "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:439:- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** no numeric span since Kindling. Anchor academy/cache spans to events; office survey records may keep their own six-year rounding where explicitly identified as the office's. The protected S8 four-year line remains word for word under [OWNER-pending #53] and is never repeated as fact. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:448:- **C11 — "Tell Lira's family I said so"** (S24 letter to Hesk, kept by the final review). The referent is unclear: no Book 8 scene sets up Hesk carrying word to Lira's family. **Kept verbatim as source-fixed; owner to confirm intent** (it may be a callback the edition's earlier books should plant). [OWNER-pending #55]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:452:- **C15 — Rhythm (not canon).** The source runs a 21.3-word sentence mean, 19% of sentences at forty words or more, and a paragraph median of 51. The edition re-builds the sentences (§7.4), and Tier C wording stays verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:484:**Existing names stay exactly as canon has them.** Never "Halcenvane" on the page; use "the academy above Ostrand". The registry collisions are untouched (OWNER-DECISIONS #6). **Audiobook read-through list** (carried): Cleon/Cael (KLEE-on/KAYL; never in one spoken run); Span/Stair; Treswick/Ternhall (keep them out of one spoken inventory); the O-onset stack Oryn/Oxhollow/Ostrand; Pike/Fiske. Places minted by canon only: Treswick, the Deepstacks, the Sunken Span, "the court" (description), the shoulder hold, the cut, the pass. **Do not name new holds** on Oryn's route. Use Oxhollow or Thornwater, or none.
