   133	Late on the fourth day, with the bell an hour off and the lamp low, Cleon put the Hall's fourth sheet beside the board for the last time that day and sat looking at the two of them for a long while without reading either, and then said, to Karis, in a voice Cael had not heard from him — not the voice for a limit; the other one, the one a man keeps for a thing he has carried alone:
