    53	He catalogued that, because it was the whole of his function in the room and a man should know his function to the hair. The middle box, against the chamber's wall, beside the first and the third and the kit's case, lid up, so that Karis could reach the sheets in it — the fair copies, the ledger, the map, the two brass edges — without asking, and then nothing. Nothing to carry. Nothing to count. Nothing to be, in a chamber under a city, but a body that had carried a box down a stair and would carry it up again at the bell, standing against a rock wall with three other bodies while two people who could read the room began to.
