    91	He had heard himself. That was the thing Cael catalogued, because it was the thing that cost: the man had heard the sentence come out of his own mouth — a name, a rank, the Compact's own title, spoken aloud in a lane behind a Compact registry in a Compact city on the Line by a man who had resigned from it, to a clerk, to smooth a door — and had heard it land. Not as authority. The clerk had not known the name. The rank was nothing at this level; the level had no column for it, and a rank that the form has no column for is a noise. And the third thing, the thing he had heard last and understood first: that a former Archmarshal invoking the Compact inside a Compact city, in front of a clerk who kept a book, with an unranked boy at his shoulder who had a piece of paper in an office in the west that said what he was, had just come within one careful man's question of closing every door on the hill, and had been stopped from it by a defector's tradecraft and a sentence that told the clerk nothing but what the form could hold.
