   113	---
   114	
   115	*Two hundred and eighty-fifth day. Under Treswick. The Deepstacks — the old quarry under the registry, shelved, unread. Second day down. Four hands; Seln above. A hundred and thirty-six in hand; the inn paid to the week.*
   116	
   117	*Karis has been looking for this room her whole life. Cleon's been sitting in it for thirty years waiting for her. Vastin tried to open a door with his rank and nearly closed all of them — an Archmarshal's worth nothing here, which he's taking about as well as I took [SHATTERED]. Down here the stone's older than the Compact, so the Compact doesn't reach. First place inside walls I've ever stood where nobody can file me, and it's a hole under a city, and it's because everything down here is older than the machine that files. Karis says give her a week. I've got a box to carry and a promise to keep about a station upstairs. I can wait.*

