    24	
    25	It was not the reading. Oryn's hands went into a thing and followed what flowed. This did not go in. It stood outside a made thing and saw how it had been put together — saw load — as the Iron read, on a floor, had told him where a thing the weight of a cart was pushing. But the Iron read felt weight. This saw *design*: which of a maker's choices were the ones the thing stood on. He had wanted, against a post across the river, an instrument for what did not move. This was an instrument for what had been *built*, and it was standing three feet from him, in a man's hands, being used on a wall.
