    39	"Structure," Cleon said. "Not meaning. It works on a made thing — a carving, a wall, a document, a thing with a maker's choices in it. It doesn't work on a river, and it doesn't work on a man, and it doesn't work on a tree, because nobody chose where the branches went. It costs me my eyes for an hour after and nothing else. It's no use to anyone in a fight, which is why I'm Bronze at sixty and have never once minded. And it can't read. I want that understood. I've had this board ten years and I can tell you every bone in it and I cannot tell you one word it says, because it doesn't say words to me. It says *load*. The words are in the text, in a hand I can half read, and the text's your work, and I've been waiting thirty years for someone to walk in and do it."
