    35	There was a case. It hung on a strap across that man's chest, and it had hung there on every road since Ostrand, shut. Cael knew what was in it. Five of them had gone through it on a table, by a shaded lamp, on a night above Ostrand; and he had written the next morning that it did not go into a book. It had not gone into this one either.
