    62	## Chapter 27 — The Middle Gallery (day 284)
    63	
    64	**Scene 1 — the stair and the cross-way.** Present: the five, Cleon. He gives the lamp to Lira and goes down ahead without a light. Twenty-seven steps; Cael two steps below the stick. The cold; nothing moves in it. The cross-way and three mouths. The lamp goes into the middle gallery. *Changes:* they are below. *Fragments:* Anchor does not ask; he marks that.
    65	
    66	**Scene 2 — the page.** A hundred and ten strides of shelving. A light at the end and a man reading. He reads to the end of his page while five people stand under loads. Three cleared tables. Karis lays out eleven, twenty-nine, twelve. The lamp: low, a hand to the left. *Vastin:* made to wait for the first time in his life; he finds no schedule for the place.
    67	
    68	**Scene 3 — from the foot.** The looking, some hours; he does not go up for his bowl. The lamp goes from Lira to Brom. He asks how old. **"Older than [UNBOUND]," Karis said.** He goes to his shelf, looks at a thing in sacking with his back turned, comes back. **"I know that hand."** (Cleon). He writes tomorrow's card and goes to rest his eyes.
    69	
    70	**Scene 4 — a week.** At the Hall's table. `[[TIER-B: "Being believed — " … "It's the end of being able to be wrong."]]` **"Give me a week."** (Karis). Brom prices a week. Karis on the three kinds of work she has now touched: the cut rock, the dark stone laid against it, the pale walls on top (she gives no year).
    71	
    72	**Scene 5 — unfiled.** Cael walks beyond the lamp into the stacks. For the first time inside walls nobody can file him. The clerk's bell. Up; the cut at dusk (the loose tread; the dished one); the lane with the alleys gone pale; Lira on his left. The loft: Seln says who came to the door.
    73	
    74	Cael beats: unfiled; what being believed costs her; Anchor's silence. Cleon beat: the page, and the bowl he missed. Karis beat: believed.
    75	
    76	## Chapter 28 — Be Nobody (day 285)
    77	
    78	**Scene 1 — the hatch.** Second bell; gates; the cut; the yard. A porter on the bench with a frame whom Cael does not look at. The clerk's difficulty with his own book: entered once already. "The same?" He will have to send up.
    79	
    80	**Scene 2 — the name.** Vastin, verbatim: **"Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —"**. Seln stands. `[[TIER-B: Seln: "He's on the count … the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was."]]` The clerk writes *the same* and *four*. Narration: Seln did not lie, and what that cost. **"I'm sorry," Vastin said. / "Don't be sorry," Seln said. "Be nobody."**
    81	
    82	**Scene 3 — the landing.** On the inner stair's first landing Vastin stops. Cael's fellow-feeling: a word that used to be a name and is now a thing that cuts whoever holds it. He does not say much. *Fragments:* none.
    83	
    84	**Scene 4 — the lamp.** Brom, then Lira, then Cael. A hand to the left of the line. "Thirty years I've held it myself." Cleon speaks to the lamp. The second chair has been cleared.
    85	
    86	**Scene 5 — the log.** The loft. **The S10 log, verbatim.** Lira reads it. Seln will not sit on that bench again. *Fragments:* Shadow at dusk; told no.
    87	
    88	Cael beats: fellow-feeling; choosing to be a lamp; "I can wait". Vastin beat: the reflex and the apology. Seln beat: the truth and its price.
    89	
    90	## Chapter 29 — The Cart and the Board (day 286)
    91	
    92	**Scene 1 — the dray.** The yard at the second bell. The wheel; the slide; the lad's boot. Brom reads the load. *Fragments:* the read asks what it weighs; told no. Brom opens no Path.
    93	
    94	**Scene 2 — the lift.** Left shoulder under the low corner; Lira and the lad; logs under the axle; Vastin and the mule. The shoulder. The factor's offer. **"I'll think on it."** The box on the bound shoulder. **"Cart was heavier."**
    95	
    96	**Scene 3 — the stair; the board.** **"You think Karis is right? That it's all built on something?" / "I think we're about to find out." / "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch."** Below: a plank of black oak stands against the Hall's table. Counters.
    97	
    98	**Scene 4 — orders.** Bearer, carried, nothing. `[[TIER-B: "They're orders."]]` Karis asks what they order. **Limit, first unit, verbatim (Cleon).** Brom asks about the bridge and the river. **Limit, second unit, verbatim (Cleon).** Rune from outside. Brom says a name at noon; Cleon says that he said no names.
    99	
   100	**Scene 5 — the make.** `[[TIER-B: "Same make."]]` Cael's wish, noted, unsaid. Up at the bell. The debt entered.
   101	
   102	Cael beats: Brom's worth without a number; the wish; the debt he cannot order away. Brom beats: the cart; the box.
   103	
   104	## Chapter 30 — What Seln Looked At (night of 286 – day 287)
   105	
   106	**Scene 1 — the room.** The loft at night. Brom's two shoulders. Cael hears the room change shape and lets it. *Fragments:* Shadow had asked at dusk.
   107	
   108	**Scene 2 — cutaway, Seln: the roof.** How he goes. The tallest roof below the second wall. The case's weight. The registry's block; the station's light, which does not flicker.
   109	
   110	**Scene 3 — cutaway, Seln: the door.** The returns door that his old trade used; what laying a thing there is; the clerk who has seen his face and the nothing that fell; a watcher in a doorway, seen once. He decides nothing.
   111	
   112	**Scene 4 — the morning.** **"I looked at it."** (Seln). The morning log: **"Brom was offered the life. He picked up the box." / "Seln looked at it. Decided nothing."** Below: the board's figures, seen from outside Karis.
   113	
   114	**Scene 5 — four times.** Vastin and the lamp, four times, the fourth day. Cleon's week, from today.
   115	
   116	**Scene 6 — the close; the parapet.** The bundle pointed at. `[[TIER-B: Cleon's close (S11): "You've been reading the strata. … never once slept well since."]]` Up. At the parapet: **"How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either."**
   117	
   118	Cael beats: letting Seln go unasked; not there yet either. Seln beats: the walk. Vastin beat: four times. Cleon beat: the close.
   119	
   120	## Chapter 31 — One at a Time (night of 287 – day 289)
   121	
   122	**Scene 1 — cutaway, Karis: the loft, night of the 287th.** What she was told at the day's end and what she will not do with it. Her method: figures first.
   123	
   124	**Scene 2 — cutaway, Karis: the 288th, forenoon.** The test of the number-words against the old ledgers. Eight letters. The cushion.
   125	
   126	**Scene 3 — cutaway, Karis: the 288th, afternoon.** Letters from the Ring, the Stair, the Hall. The bundle stays on its shelf; the page stays in her coat; her refusal.
   127	
   128	**Scene 4 — looked at (288th, evening).** Seln: the same boots twice. The route kept. Vastin moved twice today.
   129	
   130	**Scene 5 — the ladders (289th).** A hundred and thirty-four. Lira on the stacks; the drop without the arm. Brom's toes. Cael, holding the lamp, moves it before the word.
   131	
   132	Karis beats: the refusal; the letters. Lira beat: the drop. Cael beats: which way the looking runs; that he is afraid for Lira's arm and says so once.
   133	
   134	## Chapter 32 — No Round (day 290)
   135	
   136	**Scene 1 — the fourth bell.** The last hour below; fourteen letters; the bell; the yard at dusk; the order of climbing.
   137	
   138	**Scene 2 — both ends.** The gate; two staves. Vastin turns uphill. Four; the bow; the lantern at the rail. The stick comes down. No round.
   139	
