9:- Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date. Seln went still at the date and said only "I have read it."
20:4. **The technician's date is never printed.** The office that keeps the stations opens its year on a different day from the seat's registry, so a station's "year and day" must be turned before it can be laid beside a registry date; Vastin gives the difference while reading the abstracts for procedure, and the page does not give the number. Cael turns it and comes out on the date that has stood at the head of his own file on every desk since his Kindling. No span is computed. He does not write it.
26:## The sums that must add up on the page
44:2. **Hands.** Cael gives the ruling that he promised, in daylight: he is ruling on a cut and says why. Lira: she saw the end of that move the night before. Five hands. Pike will not write a clearance taken without a healer named. Oryn, from the wash-house door: the mill has waited a cold term; she will go round by the top. **Pike writes a sixth line for the healer**, the first column he has ever had for her. Vastin pays the keeper for the loft and gets up.
75:1. **Daylight.** Six rows under pebbles. Karis counts every row and writes the figures. Five groups of signs in every row: "Five." Four she can lay against the hide by their measures. Oryn will not come to the slab.
83:1. **Seln (cutaway).** The night of the 277th from inside: a date under a pencil, and a file that he had copied the head of. The turn done in his head. This morning he draws the sheet out of the second row to do it properly, against the abstracts' own day column. It comes out as it did.
84:2. **Seln (cutaway).** What he will not do: say it; write it; guess. What it costs to give a thing without saying it. The case on his chest is not thought about. The boy counts a row short and goes white. He sets the sheet down, and goes to the water so as not to watch.
85:3. **The sum.** Cael reads the date for the first time. He turns it. He does it twice. He knows the day. He does not put a verb to it. His hand goes to Hesk's book and comes away. He lays the sheet back at the foot of the second row. "I've read it."
92:2. **The term.** **"Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second."** Five holds, and down onto the mill from above. **"Three weeks"** (Seln). The sentence that she swallowed three times: the station. He writes it in the log and reads it back.
138:- **Ch18:** the date is a registry date laid against a registry date, by Seln and then by Cael, with no arithmetic. Vastin names the town at the close.

